## Capture Tcl — do
- One small command at a time (or `execute_tcl_batch` with ~50–100 ms delay); always trailing `\n`
- Wire with `GetOffsetHotSpot` ÷ 100 (inches); pin-tip to pin-tip
- Grounds: `PlaceGround` capsym `"0"` `"0"`; place so hotspot X aligns (hs ≈ loc + 0.1"); wire **straight down from above**; rot 0
- Prefer design-cache / known libs after warm-up place; verify with part count
- Delete **one** `DeletePartInst` / `DeleteGlobal` / `DeleteWire` at a time
- Create sim profiles in Capture UI (**PSpice → New Simulation Profile**), then edit `.sim` on disk — do not rely on hand-edited `.opj` GUIDs alone (invalid GUID = silent drop; Capture overwrites `.opj` on save)

## Capture Tcl — don't
- Bulk `DeletePartInst`, `Edit::Select All` + Delete, `BringToFront`
- `PlacePart` on `marker.etc` / advanced markers via Tcl (hangs/crashes)
- `SetLocation` on ground globals (crash)
- Fairchild `2N7000` + `SetEffectiveProp` Reference (crash) — use `MbreakN` + MODEL `2N7000`
- Giant `source` scripts / CorSimSrvr / ASP `orTclNewSimProfile` (needs registered client)
- Bare `V(VOUT)` in `.PRINT`/`.PROBE` — PSpice treats as **device**; use `V([VOUT])` or numeric nodes `V(3)`

## PSpice profiles
- Register: create in UI first, then patch `.sim`
- Headless run: `C:\Cadence\OrCADX_25.1\tools\bin\psp_cmd.exe` with absolute `.lib` paths; kill process after `JOB CONCLUDED` (may hang on Probe)
- `sim_lib.ParametricSettings` encodes Lab5 UI parametric block

